From 8b3dd077d80b74d941e86bd33bddcf2e36842544 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 19:13:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] PS5: compile the POSIX sources for the console

- The POSIX-only sources accept REX_PLATFORM_PS5.
- The SDK's libc++ 18, like Apple's, has no floating-point std::from_chars
  and no clock_time_conversion: the PS5 takes the macOS shims (numeric.h,
  chrono.h). newlocale and strtod_l come from the SDK's libc and platform layer.
- FreeBSD's off_t and struct stat are 64-bit, with no *64 variants; it has
  CLOCK_MONOTONIC_PRECISE rather than CLOCK_MONOTONIC_RAW, and endian.h under
  sys/.
- No libraries are loaded at run time (dynlib.h names), no native window
  surface yet (window_sdl.cpp), BSD sockets for XAM's networking, and
  RenderDoc's header accepts the platform.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0136zBnRC7dbQro6PQoycWYT
